WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.662
Servers have no Group Policy analytics.

2
00:00:02.662 --> 00:00:07.953
Microsoft publishes no tool that imports
a GPO into machine configuration,

3
00:00:07.953 --> 00:00:11.563
but it does publish a path,
and the program follows it.

4
00:00:11.563 --> 00:00:16.375
Step one, audit beside Group Policy:
let Group Policy keep enforcing while

5
00:00:16.375 --> 00:00:21.425
Azure Policy audits the same settings,
then move enforcement over gradually.

6
00:00:21.425 --> 00:00:22.588
Two cautions.

7
00:00:22.588 --> 00:00:25.455
Azure Policy settings
don't show up in gpresult,

8
00:00:25.455 --> 00:00:28.175
so the compliance reports
become the record.

9
00:00:28.175 --> 00:00:32.363
And per-user settings, like mapped
drives, stay with Group Policy.

10
00:00:32.363 --> 00:00:36.050
Step two, start from the built-in
baselines and definitions,

11
00:00:36.050 --> 00:00:39.287
which cover many settings
with no conversion at all.

12
00:00:39.287 --> 00:00:43.963
Step three, package what's left with
Microsoft's GuestConfiguration module;

13
00:00:43.963 --> 00:00:47.450
a package that applies settings
needs a recent Arc agent.

14
00:00:47.450 --> 00:00:50.366
Step four, treat a
converted GPO as a draft,

15
00:00:50.366 --> 00:00:55.512
because the conversion command is
community-supported, not Microsoft's.

16
00:00:55.512 --> 00:00:58.920
Test it in audit mode before
anything enforces it.
